<figure aria-labelledby="process-caption">
  <ol class="lifecycle">
    <li>
      <span class="phase">Foundation</span>
      <strong>Validate sources and establish comparison grain</strong>
      <small>Confirm what each record represents before combining evidence.</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="phase">Preparation</span>
      <strong>Profile and normalize evidence</strong>
      <small>Expose missing, inconsistent, or ambiguous inputs for review.</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="phase">Governance</span>
      <strong>Apply governed rules and readiness decisions</strong>
      <small>Keep proposed treatments separate from accepted business rules.</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="phase">Analysis</span>
      <strong>Produce controlled analysis outputs</strong>
      <small>Allow results to proceed, remain in review, or stop safely.</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="phase">Assurance</span>
      <strong>Reconcile results and review exceptions</strong>
      <small>Connect summary conclusions to checks and unresolved evidence.</small>
    </li>
    <li>
      <span class="phase">Handoff</span>
      <strong>Package results for stakeholder use</strong>
      <small>Provide reviewable outputs, operating guidance, and clear limits.</small>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <figcaption id="process-caption" class="caption">
    An independently designed, data-free lifecycle showing how analytical evidence can
    move from source review to governed stakeholder use. It does not depict the employer
    application, architecture, rules, or results.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
